# The constellation model

stellario's memory is organized by naming, not by registry. A slug's
family lives in a `.stella/` directory: the canonical `<slug>.stella`
(lint-disciplined, indexed) and drafts `<slug>.<star>` (loose form,
gitignored — the extension IS the canonical claim). Demotion is losing
the extension; a vacant canonical slot is an open question, not an
error. Capsules emerge from sync targeting them — structure is
discovered from writing, never declared.

<stellario>
